<title>CHINA: China's Jan 1997 edible oil buying detailed.</title>
<headline>China's Jan 1997 edible oil buying detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows import figures for three edible oils of five major Chinese customs offices as well as the country of origin to date in 1997.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 percent because details of some smaller import regions and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>------SOYOIL</p>
<p>Jan imports  182,251</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     Jan	  Pct</p>
<p>    Shanghai	41,024	22.5</p>
<p>    Huangpu	 16,706	 9.2</p>
<p>    Tianjin	 59,250	32.5</p>
<p>    Nanjing	 22,501	12.3</p>
<p>    Jiulong	 20,043	11.0</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Brazil	  61,952	34.0</p>
<p>    Argentina     20,000	11.0</p>
<p>    U.S.	    89,469	49.1</p>
<p>    Malaysia	10,701	 5.9</p>
<p>------PALM OIL</p>
<p>    Jan imports   67,241</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     Jan	  Pct</p>
<p>    Jiulong	 15,211	22.6</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>    Shantou	 13,534	20.1</p>
<p>    Nanning	  8,464	12.6</p>
<p>    Huangpu	  4,862	 7.2</p>
<p>    Zhanjiang     14,521	21.7</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Malaysia	61,144	90.9</p>
<p>    Indonesia	3,448	 5.1</p>
<p>------RAPESEED OIL</p>
<p>    Jan imports   32,094</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     Jan	  Pct</p>
<p>    Jiulong	 23,986	74.7</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>    Zhanjiang	4,054	12.6</p>
<p>    Nanning	  3,152	 9.8</p>
<p>    Shantou	    352	 1.1</p>
<p>    Jiangmen	   301	 0.9</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Germany	 19,172	59.7</p>
<p>    Malaysia	   152	 0.5</p>
<p>    Netherlands   11,856	36.9</p>
<p>    Canada	     320	 1.0</p>
<p>    Singapore	  162	 0.5</p>
</text>
